rable"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns the least-weight Hamiltonian cycle of the simple graph, or nil when there is none;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"among the optimal ones, the lexicographically least by vertex number listed from the first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex. The graph need not be complete: a missing pair is an absent edge. Tours read the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"simple graph, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":" documents; nil below three vertices."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tour is determined for integer weights. With floating-point weights it is optimal for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sums as computed, and chosen by the same rule on them, so which of several equal tours","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comes out, and its orientation, can depend on rounding.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The table, 2ⁿ⁻¹ · (n − 1) weights and as many validity bytes, fits in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"4 GiB: at most 25 vertices with 8-byte weights, 26 with 4-byte ones; no weight is NaN or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"infinite; the sum along any path fits in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Θ(2ⁿ n²) time and Θ(2ⁿ n) memory: n = 20 takes 80 MB of table for 8-byte"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"weights on a complete graph, and 90 MB on another (the validity flags)."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The shortest tour, by Held–Karp dynamic programming (Bellman 1962; Held and Karp 1962)."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/shortesttour(weight:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"references":{"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols/Graph/shortestTour(weight:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/shortesttour(weight:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/shortestTour(weight:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"shortestTour","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cycle","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"title":"shortestTour(weight:)","role":"symb